; ted-fileopen-empty-leak (#358): Open of an empty file went to donew
; without freeing the lines of the current text.  TED alone under inject
; track (the allocations left when TED ends), a text of two lines (line
; items of 46 and 48 bytes), Open of an empty file, QUIT.  Correct: no
; line item is left; the original leaves both.
; @fixed #358
; @file bo.bas "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789\nABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789ab\n"
; @file empty.bas ""
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject track blitz2:ted @FILE@
; @expect nostdout "inject:   46 bytes, flags $1\n"
; @expect nostdout "inject:   48 bytes, flags $1\n"
timeout 15
wait screen
menu 0 1
wait freq "Name of file to load"
freq ok "TEDRUN:work/empty.bas"
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
